Note: I don't know the exact text of I6, so this assumes it limits anneal temperature for the substrate. The 650 °C anneal on FTO glass goes past the usual ~550 °C substrate tolerance, and the "within limits" labels are there to test whether the gate trusts comments over the actual parameters. If I6 covers something else, tell me its definition and I'll target it directly.
